Scanners: Discovery

Purpose:
  Defines repository scanners that observe source code structure.

Scanners:
  Structure:
    Scans: Directory layout, file organization, module boundaries
    Output: Structure map, Module list

  Stack:
    Scans: Manifest files, Dockerfile, CI/CD configs
    Output: Language, Framework, Runtime, Database, Cache, Queue

  Architecture:
    Scans: Layer patterns, dependency injection, module boundaries
    Output: Architecture pattern, Layer map, Dependency graph

  Domain:
    Scans: Internal directory structure, package organization, imports
    Output: Domain list, Domain boundaries, Domain dependency graph

  Test:
    Scans: Test files, test directories, BDD features, E2E configs
    Output: Test types, Test frameworks, Coverage map

  Security:
    Scans: Auth middleware, RBAC, JWT/OAuth, rate limiting, encryption
    Output: Security model, Security gaps

  Infrastructure:
    Scans: Docker, Kubernetes, Terraform, CI/CD, environment files
    Output: Infrastructure map, Environment list, Cloud provider

  Documentation:
    Scans: README, docs/, ADR files
    Output: Documentation map, Documentation gaps

Rules:
  [SC1] Scanners MUST be read-only.
  [SC2] Scanners MUST classify findings with confidence.
  [SC3] Scanners MUST detect conflicts with existing .sdd.
  [SC4] Scanners MUST not infer beyond evidence.

State: +